  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The denominator is positive for every integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. Multiplying by the conjugate gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The sum becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mn>0</mn></msqrt><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>99</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Every interior square root cancels.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> Only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mn>0</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math> remains. Answer D.</p>"
